.el .ds Aq '
.TH next 1  "next " 
.SH NAME
next \- List actionable work — ready plus already\-claimed, unblocked, not deferred — ranked by the active plugin\*(Aqs `next` policy and tiered to finish before starting: work you can close now, then each started epic with its open children, then the backlog. `\-\-sort id` gives the flat, untiered order; `\-\-limit` shows only the head of it, and says so
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBnext\fR [\fB\-\-now\fR] [\fB\-\-label\fR] [\fB\-\-sort\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List actionable work — ready plus already\-claimed, unblocked, not deferred — ranked by the active plugin\*(Aqs `next` policy and tiered to finish before starting: work you can close now, then each started epic with its open children, then the backlog. `\-\-sort id` gives the flat, untiered order; `\-\-limit` shows only the head of it, and says so
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-now\fR \fI<NOW>\fR
Reference time (ISO\-8601 / RFC3339); defaults to now
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fI<LABEL>\fR
Filter to ready items carrying this label (user vocabulary, not the display type)
.TP
\fB\-\-sort\fR \fI<SORT>\fR
Sort order: `rank` | `id` (default `rank`). An unknown key is a loud error
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR
Max items to show (default: no limit). Applied last — after `\-\-sort` and `\-\-label` — and never silently: a truncated list is headed `showing <n> of <total>`, and under `\-\-json` the flag wraps the records as `{"items": [...], "total": <n>}` so a consumer reads the untruncated total instead of inferring it from the array\*(Aqs length
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
